  "articleBody": "It's super frustrating when you're in the middle of a remodel, and the paint job isn't going as planned. Maybe the colors aren't quite right, or you're noticing imperfections after the first coat. A common issue we see is a vague scope definition from the get-go. If you didn't clearly outline what surfaces were included or the specific products being used, it's easy for things to go off track. Another snag can be not confirming your colors and sheen in advance, which can lead to a mismatched look or simply not loving the final result. Sometimes, folks underestimate how much prep work truly goes into a good paint job, leading to a finish that just doesn't hold up. And let's be honest, skipping a written agreement for changes, payment, or warranties can leave you feeling pretty exposed if issues arise. To avoid these headaches, make sure you have a clear, written scope of work, confirm every detail from color to sheen, and understand the prep required. If you're finding yourself in over your head with drywall repairs, multiple rooms, or intricate trim work, that's often a good sign it’s time to call in a professional like HH Remodeling LLC. We can step in, assess the situation, and get your remodel painting back on track for a smooth, beautiful finish that makes your house feel more like a home.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
